error[NK2605]: This function can fail, because `println` can fail.
  --> tests/drop_that_prints_must_catch.nika:8:9
   |
 8 |         println(f"closing {self.name}")
   |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: `println` can fail with `io::IoError`.
   = note: A call that can fail looks like any other call, so its failure passes straight through this function unless you handle it.
   = help: Handle the failure in the body (`… catch { }`), or move teardown that can fail to `impl Cleanup for File { fn cleanup(ref mut self) throws { … } }`.
1 place that can fail without saying so
